# `SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`: the cells WITHDRAWN from `topology`, each with its own
# named diagnostic. A word withdrawn from one genre is not an unknown word,
# and `"threshold" is not allowed in genre topology` on its own would send an
# author looking for a typo — so every message states the ground of ITS cell,
# because the grounds differ:
#
#   threshold  a threshold in this genre's domain is a QUEUE DEPTH WITH A
#              NUMERIC VALUE (RFC 2309 minth/maxth, RFC 7567), while
#              FigDown's takes no value= at all. Zero occurrences.
#   band       a BAND here is a frequency band — radio, wireless, microwave,
#              optical transport — which is exactly the figure a topology
#              document draws. Its two occurrences were both fixtures.
#
# The KEEP half of the grid for this genre is 240.
#
# The last line is a DIFFERENT diagnostic and is here deliberately. `plane`
# is not a per-genre withdrawal: `PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT` removes it from the LANGUAGE, so it
# joins the retired-keyword sweep AHEAD of the genre allowlist and reports
# the same message in every genre, including `bitfield`/`table`/`timing`.
# `topology`'s share of that claim sits here rather than with the rest,
# because this is where every authored `plane` in the tree was written —
# `examples/evpn-fabric.fd` had `plane overlay "VXLAN tunnels" z-index=2`,
# where `overlay` is itself a networking term, so the line read as a
# network-architectural assertion and was in fact a paint order. The other
# seven genres are `918-withdrawn-plane-keyword` (NORMATIVE: `block`,
# `bitfield`, `table`) and `919-withdrawn-plane-experimental-genres`
# (`flowchart`, `statechart`, the `timing` genre header).
figdown 0.1 topology
node a "A"
group g "G"
threshold "Budget" 60% in=g
band "Window" 10..20% in=g
plane overlay "VXLAN tunnels" z-index=2
